{"name":"Skylark","hex":"#c1e4f0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skylark","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small brown passerine bird, Alauda arvensis, that sings as it flies high into the air."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To jump about joyfully, frolic; to play around, play tricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skylark"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skylark (Canadian band)","blocks":[{"text":"Skylark was a Canadian pop and rock band active from 1971 to 1973 and based in Vancouver. \"Wildflower\" is their biggest hit."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skylark_(Canadian_band)"},{"title":"Skylark (rocket)","blocks":[{"text":"Skylark was a family of British sounding rockets. It was operational between 1957 and 2005."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Skylark_launch.jpg/330px-Skylark_launch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skylark_(rocket)"},{"title":"Alauda","blocks":[{"text":"Alauda is a genus of larks found across much of Europe, Asia and in the mountains of north Africa, with one species endemic to the islet of Raso in the Cape Verde Islands. At least two additional species are known from the fossil record. The genus name is from Latin alauda, \"lark\". Pliny the Elder thought the word was originally of Celtic origin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Alauda_arvensis_2.jpg/330px-Alauda_arvensis_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alauda"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Skylark_launch_for_NASA.tiff/lossless-page1-500px-Skylark_launch_for_NASA.tiff.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Skylark_launch_for_NASA.tiff/lossless-page1-500px-S